.TH SFREE 1 "September 2026" "sfree 1.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sfree \- display Linux memory and swap usage
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sfree
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sfree
reads
.I /proc/meminfo
and displays memory, swap, and total usage.
By default it prints a colored table that adapts to the terminal width.
It can also print machine-readable JSON or output compatible with common
.BR free (1)
options.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --json
Print machine-readable JSON with memory, swap, and combined total objects.
.TP
.BI --unit " UNIT"
Force the output unit. Supported values are
.BR auto ,
.BR B ,
.BR kB ,
.BR KiB ,
.BR MB ,
.BR MiB ,
.BR GB ,
.BR GiB ,
.BR TB ,
.BR TiB ,
.BR PB ,
and
.BR PiB .
.TP
.BI --color " WHEN"
Control ANSI color output in the default table.
.I WHEN
can be
.BR always ,
.BR auto ,
or
.BR never .
The default is
.BR always .
.TP
.B --human
Use automatic human-readable units. This is the default in table and JSON mode.
.TP
.BR -b , " --bytes"
Show values in bytes in free-compatible output.
.TP
.BR --kilo , " --mega" , " --giga" , " --tera" , " --peta"
Show values in decimal kilobytes, megabytes, gigabytes, terabytes, or petabytes.
.TP
.BR -k , " --kibi"
Show values in kibibytes.
.TP
.BR -m , " --mebi"
Show values in mebibytes.
.TP
.BR -g , " --gibi"
Show values in gibibytes.
.TP
.BR --tebi , " --pebi"
Show values in tebibytes or pebibytes.
.TP
.B -h
Show human-readable free-compatible output.
Unlike many commands, help is only available through
.BR --help
so that
.B -h
matches
.BR free (1)
behavior.
.TP
.B --si
Use powers of 1000 instead of powers of 1024 for human-readable output.
.TP
.BR -l , " --lohi"
Show high and low memory rows when the kernel exposes them.
.TP
.BR -L , " --line"
Show output on a single line.
.TP
.BR -t , " --total"
Show the combined RAM plus swap total row.
.TP
.BR -v , " --committed"
Show commit limit and committed memory.
.TP
.BI -s " N" , " --seconds " N
Repeat output every
.I N
seconds.
.TP
.BI -c " N" , " --count " N
Repeat output
.I N
times and then exit.
.TP
.B --help
Show help and exit.
.TP
.BR -V , " --version"
Show version information and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B COLUMNS
Used as a fallback terminal width when stdout is not attached to a TTY.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disables ANSI color output unless colors are explicitly forced by future modes.
.TP
.B SUPERFREE_MEMINFO
Override the meminfo path. This is primarily intended for automated tests.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Show the adaptive default table:
.B sfree
.TP
Print JSON in MiB:
.B sfree --json --unit MiB
.TP
Print free-compatible wide byte output with totals:
.B sfree --bytes --total --wide
.TP
Print a compact one-line output with committed memory:
.B sfree --line --bytes --total --committed
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /proc/meminfo
Kernel memory information read by
.BR sfree .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Runtime error, such as being unable to read meminfo.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command-line option or option value.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR free (1),
.BR proc_meminfo (5)
.SH AUTHORS
sfree is maintained by Javier Molinero.
